   "flags": [],
   "note": "Uncertainty (+/-0.006 A) covers numerical EOS fit form/window spread (5.4654-5.4672 A), agreement between EOS fit and stress-based relaxation (5.4674 A), and the model's deviation from its PBE reference for Si (MACE 5.466 vs PBE 5.472 A). It does NOT cover the systematic error of the PBE functional relative to experiment: the result is a static-lattice PBE-quality value and is ~0.65% above the measured CODATA lattice parameter 5.431020511(89) A at 22.5 C (NIST CODATA 2018 X-ray table), and ~0.8% above a zero-point-corrected experimental value (~5.421 A, as tabulated in arXiv:2601.11177). Zero-point and thermal expansion are not included (static calculation). Validation (same model/protocol): MACE-MPA-0 vs literature PBE: Si 5.466 vs 5.472, Al 4.037 vs 4.042, Cu 3.639 vs 3.642, C 3.578 vs 3.571, Ge 5.720 vs 5.765 (PBE values as tabulated in arXiv:2601.11177 and arXiv:2604.07046, retrieved via web search). Bulk modulus 88.4 GPa. Si is in the MACE-MPA-0 training domain (MPtrj/sAlex PBE data), so the Si-vs-PBE comparison is not fully independent; Al/Cu/C give out-of-sample confirmation of the protocol. The tier1 calibration file contains no lattice-constant records, so it was not used.",
